# Transitive dependencies:

# filelock 3.32.4: the fix is 4.2.1, a major-version move. filelock 4.x changes
# UnixFileLock's behaviour on shared lock directories (4.2.12 refuses, with
# PermissionError, a lock file another account owns under a sticky parent), and these
# steps share one HF cache across accounts on group-shared filesystems. That move belongs
# in its own change, tested on the cluster (#752); pyproject.toml holds it with a
# filelock<4 constraint. Not reachable: the flaw is only in ReadWriteLock /
# AsyncReadWriteLock (the SQLite-backed lock, added in 3.20.4), and nothing in the image
# uses them -- no module in the venv outside filelock itself names ReadWriteLock (checked
# in the vllm 0.26.0 / torch 2.11.0 image, 2026-11-23), and the distill code has none.
# Until 2027-05-31.
